.TH LARGEFILES 1 "October 2026" "SASD Freeware" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
largefiles \- locate large regular files in a directory tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B largefiles
.RB [ --min-size " SIZE" ]
.RB [ --top " N" ]
.RB [ --all ]
.RB [ --null ]
.RB [ --one-file-system ]
.I DIRECTORY
.SH DESCRIPTION
Scan a directory tree without following symbolic links. By default report the
50 largest regular files of at least 100 MiB. All matching files are counted.
Text output escapes control characters in filenames.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --min-size " SIZE"
Minimum file size in bytes or binary K/M/G/T suffix, inclusive.
.TP
.BI --top " N"
Keep at most N largest results (1 to 10000; default 50).
.TP
.B --all
Stream all matching files, unsorted.
.TP
.B --null
Output NUL-separated pairs of size and raw pathname, without header or totals.
.TP
.B --one-file-system
Skip entries on other device IDs.
.TP
.B --help
Show usage.
.TP
.B --version
Show version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 complete; 1 traversal errors; 2 invalid options; 3 invalid root directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fs-report (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR du (1)
